    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71671304\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p><span class=\"drop-caps\">W</span>here are the role models who help youngsters imbibe values? The brain has an enormous capacity for imitation. It is through imitation much learning takes place. Children pick up language and skills through imitation. There is an old saying, “See good; hear good; speak good.” Whatever good we see, hear, and speak will be stored in the brain, even subliminally. But gone are the days when people were surrounded only by those who possess good values, behaviour, and character.</p><p>There were excellent teachers who not only preached values but also lived them. There were political leaders with social responsibility who were role models through their words and deeds. There were truthful national leaders whose actions brought laurels to the nation. They offered themselves as models.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 08, 2026 04:35 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71671304\" data-title=\"Finding role models\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/finding-role-models/article71671304.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-cacc54651f61d09c124093cc-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/finding-role-models/article71671304.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=Finding%20role%20models&amp;amp;body=C