    "image_url": null,
    "image_caption": null,
    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71671253\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p><span class=\"drop-caps\">I</span> was born in 1988, too late to remember the 1980s and too early to grow up with the Internet. Yet much of my childhood in a small town still carried the unhurried character of that decade. Discotheques and frantic car chases were strictly Tier 1 phenomena. For children growing up in small-town India, excitement had a very different scale.</p><p>The air was cleaner, traffic was sparse, and summer nights could still be spent sleeping on open terraces under starry skies. An evening did not need a restaurant reservation, a multiplex or a digital itinerary. One could simply sit outside after dinner and watch the night unfold. The occasional scooter, a distant train or a barking dog was enough to interrupt the silence.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 08, 2026 04:20 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71671253\" data-title=\"The lost luxury\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/the-lost-luxury/article71671253.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-c2da51fa531eac1a71035fa7-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/the-lost-luxury/article71671253.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=The%20lost%20luxury&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2