    "content_text": "I\nwas born in 1988, too late to remember the 1980s and too early to grow up with the Internet. Yet much of my childhood in a small town still carried the unhurried character of that decade. Discotheques and frantic car chases were strictly Tier 1 phenomena. For children growing up in small-town India, excitement had a very different scale.\nThe air was cleaner, traffic was sparse, and summer nights could still be spent sleeping on open terraces under starry skies. An evening did not need a restaurant reservation, a multiplex or a digital itinerary. One could simply sit outside after dinner and watch the night unfold. The occasional scooter, a distant train or a barking dog was enough to interrupt the silence.\nPublished\n- November 08, 2026 04:20 am IST\nCopy link\nEmail\nFacebook\nTwitter\nTelegram\nLinkedIn\nWhatsApp\nReddit\nREAD LATER\nSEE ALL\nRemove",
