    "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/what-are-friends-for/article71653483.ece",
    "title": "What are friends for",
    "subtitle": null,
    "author": "J.R.K.  Rao",
    "published_at": null,
    "image_url": null,
    "image_caption": null,
    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71653483\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p>Many imagine that they know a great many people; yet, in reality, they are often no more than a passing thought in the lives of those others, seldom occupying their mindspace in their quotidian existence.</p><p>Bertrand Russell observed, “Don’t expect others to take as much interest in you as you do yourself. And don’t imagine that most people give enough thought to you to have any special desire to persecute you.” In essence, he suggests that human beings habitually assume that others are thinking about them far more than they actually are — a narcissistic tendency that constantly seeks to reinforce self-image and self-esteem.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 08, 2026 03:20 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71653483\" data-title=\"What are friends for\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/what-are-friends-for/article71653483.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-675345ac1cf672d4e16cf58b-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/what-are-friends-for/article71653483.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=What%20are%20friends%20for&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Fwhat-are-friends-for%2Farticle71653483.ece\" target=\"_self\">\n                    Email     \n  